  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "6743c02b5ffcf24a0ba12da40b2512ff176986ec",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6743c02b5ffcf24a0ba12da40b2512ff176986ec",
      "message": "Merge the pre-launch dispute rows: staging held past case expiry raises a named alarm",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T15:46:03Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "64c510bdd034d0930864434e9fc06585c23a0eff",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/64c510bdd034d0930864434e9fc06585c23a0eff",
      "message": "Pin the Cardano node 11.1.3 release tarballs in the Nix route",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T15:26:33Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "eda4533e3b095ae170c4f3571d686f6c95b4c92c",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/eda4533e3b095ae170c4f3571d686f6c95b4c92c",
      "message": "Keep the Cardano node socket reachable by host tools on the Kupmios stack\n\nThe node creates its socket as root with mode 0755, so the host-side\nprovider preflight could not connect. The health check now reapplies 0666\non every check, as the devnet scripts do, which also covers node restarts.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T15:21:19Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "4e421fc22fce47a5b5258cb74cbe46de7ed8d7ff",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/4e421fc22fce47a5b5258cb74cbe46de7ed8d7ff",
      "message": "Ship identity as the DA payload envelope default the node accepts\n\nThe example env and the kill-recovery acceptance set the envelope to off,\nwhich the node has refused since only identity and zstd remain, so a stack\nbuilt from the example stopped at provider preflight.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T15:17:29Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "f57df6f4b7ad30ee4890d86cdbd925323c7c9d6f",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/f57df6f4b7ad30ee4890d86cdbd925323c7c9d6f",
      "message": "Merge the staging alarm past a case expiry",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T15:11:16Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "6a3a8b5975fb822441df2fb6d456cffac4b03eb9",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6a3a8b5975fb822441df2fb6d456cffac4b03eb9",
      "message": "Name staging outputs held past a case's expiry under reconciliation-only\n\nUnder reconciliation-only authority, a thread of ours at the PrepareSelected\nmove's holder or past it keeps the staging outputs it needs, so it can go on\nif the header comes back. That hold lasts until the thread leaves its\nholders or the case closes, whoever sends it. Once the case's expiry has\npassed with such a thread standing, a run that would only wait now reports\nthose outputs, with their lovelace and the expiry, under the named alarm\nvalidation-trace-staging-held-past-expiry. The alarm sends and signs nothing\nnew.\n\nRows for both positions check two things. Past the case's expiry, each run\nreports the alarm and the outputs stay live. Once the other party closes the\ncase, each output is spent back to our wallet and is final at release depth\nbefore the run ends.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T15:11:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "89ab918f2f55c24eb26ddb5bc36389e43591bc61",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/89ab918f2f55c24eb26ddb5bc36389e43591bc61",
      "message": "Merge the narrowed differing-staging row",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:44:32Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "e425c12a2bda2f20631e7ded691d97e2a6fd4a08",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/e425c12a2bda2f20631e7ded691d97e2a6fd4a08",
      "message": "Narrow the differing-staging row to what it pins\n\nThe row's runner reads our journal as it stood before a run was staged\nagain. That journal shows none of our moves that read a staging, so its\nsweep would spend those outputs back. The test holds those spend backs as a\nwait. The row now claims only the one-step alarm with the differing text,\nand that no move is built from that window. It drops the liveness check that\nheld only because of the test's hold.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:44:24Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ee91c6a93af304b3b3353aa3314da4b805de503d",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ee91c6a93af304b3b3353aa3314da4b805de503d",
      "message": "Merge the bData boundary comment",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:27:34Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "66b6a91bfa6c85c5f9e010c12b8a742309b74eb2",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/66b6a91bfa6c85c5f9e010c12b8a742309b74eb2",
      "message": "Name the direct payload bound constant in the bData boundary rows\n\nThe rows keep 9,215 as a literal, so a change to the bound turns them red\ninstead of moving with it.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:27:27Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "e509d7f1aa982f47dc038ca2d48083609fd74dfc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/e509d7f1aa982f47dc038ca2d48083609fd74dfc",
      "message": "Create the Kupo snapshot directory before Docker starts the providers too\n\nThe Kupo snapshot bootstrap runs as the same unprivileged user and failed the\nsame way on a root-owned cardano/kupo.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:09:04Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "8b3f5b8457d151c2f3418830103c8a82d14f9476",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/8b3f5b8457d151c2f3418830103c8a82d14f9476",
      "message": "Merge the staged step grace-wait and differing-staging rows",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:08:09Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "29e003eee390d38bc71778f08c9d7e21fb47c231",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/29e003eee390d38bc71778f08c9d7e21fb47c231",
      "message": "Merge the equalsData and bData boundary rows",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:08:09Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "34abdf00747f356f124ca5d93bd8865a6deade37",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/34abdf00747f356f124ca5d93bd8865a6deade37",
      "message": "Create the Cardano database directory before Docker starts the providers\n\nOn a fresh checkout Docker created cardano/db as root when it created the\nnode container, and the unprivileged Mithril bootstrap then failed to move\nthe restored snapshot into it.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:04:25Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "b476608652b1293b24352e7ed2b7959b9d237db1",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/b476608652b1293b24352e7ed2b7959b9d237db1",
      "message": "Add equalsData False rows and bData rows at the direct payload bound\n\nRun each staged equalsData shape (append, slice, encodeUtf8) both ways.\nAgainst the direct constant of the same bytes, a claimed False is refused.\nAgainst other bytes of the same length, a correct False is accepted and a\nclaimed True is refused.\n\nAdd bData rows on each side of the direct payload bound. A string whose\npayload CBOR is 9,215 bytes is accepted inline. A string whose payload CBOR\nis 9,216 bytes is accepted by its leaf and refused inline. A result over\nother bytes is refused on both sides. The executor rows check how the\nargument is carried at each length.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-11-01T14:04:00Z"
    }
  ],
